mately 6999 BCE and serves as a pivotal point in understanding early urban civilization. This site, known for its strategic position along ancient trade routes connecting Egypt and Mesopotamia, has been instrumental in revealing the socio-political dynamics of early agricultural societies. The remains of fortified structures, storerooms, and ritual sites indicate a complex urban center that flourished long before the rise of more recognized ancient civilizations such as those in Mesopotamia and the Nile Valley.

